NAME
       shuf - print lines in random order

SYNOPSIS
       shuf [-n COUNT] [FILE]
       shuf -i LOW-HIGH [-n COUNT]
       shuf -e WORD...

DESCRIPTION
       shuf prints the lines of its input in a random order. It can also mix
       a range of numbers or the words on its command line.

OPTIONS
       -n, --head-count N
              Print at most N lines.

       -i, --input-range LOW-HIGH
              Shuffle the numbers from LOW to HIGH.

       -e, --echo
              Shuffle the arguments.

EXAMPLES
           shuf -n 1 /usr/share/dict/words
           shuf -i 1-100 -n 3

SEE ALSO
       sort(1), seq(1)
